From 80b9f58173afb59c2b123a20e5955afb147350c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 08:17:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Overhaul HTML report content per user feedback on real
 generated reports

Drop the "What this report is, and is not" box and the "Method and
provenance" section - both only repeated what the README/CLI banner
already say. The one load-bearing sentence from the box (coincidence
in time is not evidence of causation) moves into the Summary's opening
paragraph instead of being lost.

Enrich the Summary with actual findings instead of just methodology:
candidate count and top day, a significance read (z-score, permutation
p-value, threshold-robustness fraction), and - backed by a new
flagging_diagnostics() in eventstudy.py - real counts for why the rest
of the window's days aren't candidates (busy/toned coverage with an
ordinary move, an unusual move with ordinary coverage, an unusual move
with no coverage collected at all, or routine on both counts).

Make the timeline chart self-explanatory without hovering: SVG <title>
tooltips don't survive PDF/print/screenshot contexts, so each numbered
badge now carries an always-visible dated label, and an in-chart
caption explains what the badges and panels mean.

Attach real article data to each candidate day: Incident.headlines is
now a list of dicts (source, headline, url, sentiment_label, relevance,
summary) instead of bare strings, rendered as a link to the original
article (URL-scheme-checked before rendering) plus a real one-to-two
sentence summary from the source's own meta description or an excerpt
of the extracted body. A new per-category mechanism paragraph in
incident_narrative() explains, generically, why that kind of news
(earnings, regulatory, leadership, litigation, M&A, capital, product,
macro) plausibly moves a price the way it did - a mechanism, not a
claim about the specific article.

Adds tests/test_narrative.py (direct coverage for _drop_explanation,
_significance_paragraph, the mechanism paragraph, and the enriched
summary opening - previously only exercised indirectly), a new
TestFlaggingDiagnostics class in test_eventstudy.py, and new chart
caption/badge-date tests in test_report.py. 366 tests passing, up from
333.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
